# REST API Rules (ADR-011)

## Every Custom Endpoint

- Register on `rest_api_init` with a versioned namespace. Custom BingoCommerce
  APIs use a versioned namespace; the exact initial namespace/version is
  selected during the API-contract design — not locked in this pass.
- EVERY route has an explicit `permission_callback` performing a real check —
  `__return_true` on a mutating or data-exposing endpoint is rejected.
- EVERY parameter has `sanitize_callback` (and `validate_callback` where
  applicable).
- Normal endpoint-owned `$wpdb` queries use `$wpdb->prepare()`. REST
  controllers should call canonical domain/services rather than reimplement
  protected persistence logic. If a called canonical service is governed by
  ADR-025, that service retains its approved direct-mysqli transaction
  transport — a REST endpoint must never bypass or duplicate ADR-025 merely
  to perform database work directly. Raw interpolation remains prohibited.
- Errors return safe messages — never expose SQL, stack traces, payment
  details, or secret material.

## Machine Authentication

- WooCommerce-specific integrations (POS sync): WooCommerce REST API Consumer
  Keys, scoped per integration with explicit Read / Write / Read-Write.
- Non-WooCommerce REST integrations: WordPress core Application Passwords
  (revocable per application).
- NEVER build custom API-key auth systems for machine clients (ADR-011 /
  anti-pattern list).

## Portal Integration (ADR-035)

- The approved sequence is authenticated Portal read API, initial/full pull,
  proven idempotent Hall/Game-Type/Session-template mapping, then Portal
  webhooks and reconciliation. Do not implement or skip ahead to webhooks
  before the pull/mapping increment is proven.
- Portal endpoint paths, credentials, payloads, webhook signatures, replay/
  ordering/retry rules, and reconciliation contracts are deferred. ADR-035 does
  not authorize inventing them. ADR-011 still governs any future
  BingoCommerce-owned REST endpoint.
- Only Sessions satisfying `bingo_sessions.hall_id == mapped halls.id` are
  eligible. Do not use an `allSessions()`-equivalent source; received/shared
  Sessions are excluded from v1 Commerce sync. Portal Session `days` must not
  drive scheduling, generate occurrences, or constrain/validate Commerce
  scheduling in v1; later advisory validation requires a separately approved
  requirement.

## Android Device API (QR redemption)

- `caller_id` is unique per tablet and is BingoCommerce's confirmed tablet
  identity concept for redemption purposes (BR-045). Exact device-
  authentication credentials, device-registry persistence, table scope,
  status fields, last-seen tracking, and lifecycle belong to the upcoming
  Android/API technical design — not locked here. ADR-018 governs custom-
  table naming/prefix conventions; it does not itself require a network-wide
  device registry. ADR-011 remains authoritative for machine authentication
  generally — do not invent a new custom token scheme or token lifetime in
  this pass.
- Redemption is server-authoritative and acts on the authoritative
  entitlement/ticket state produced after successful online payment
  confirmation (BR-043, BR-053). It conceptually validates: ticket/
  entitlement validity; hall/tenant; Session; tablet/caller identity;
  refund/cancellation/void state where applicable; BR-045/BR-055 Game-Type
  accumulation limits; and authorization/security requirements. A valid QR
  remains redeemable after Session start (BR-056) — do not invent a
  must-redeem-before-start rule or an automatic close from Session-name
  text. Do not re-check a specific WooCommerce payment-status name at
  redemption. Do not lock a specific device-binding column, expiration
  field, or `issued` -> `redeemed` implementation transition here — those
  belong to a later dedicated entitlement/redemption persistence design, not
  ADR-031's Catalog/Session persistence design.
- Redemption accumulation (BR-045, BR-055) MUST be atomic/concurrency-safe: existing
  hall/session/caller/Game-Type accumulation + incoming Package entitlement <=
  current effective limit, checked and mutated atomically. Multiple valid
  Digital Packages for the same Session may redeem onto the same tablet and
  accumulate independently by Game Type. If any affected Game Type would
  exceed its effective limit, reject the ENTIRE incoming receipt — no
  partial redemption. Do not reintroduce shared checkout/Session-capacity
  accounting (retired per BR-041/ADR-028).
- One digital ticket binds to one Android tablet/device (BR-009, BR-044). A
  retry of the SAME logical redemption operation after a timeout or lost
  response must be handled idempotently and must never apply the
  entitlement twice. A genuinely NEW redemption attempt for an already-bound
  ticket on another device is blocked unless an authorized BR-010
  staff-gated reactivation makes the ticket eligible for recovery — the
  exact reactivation mechanism belongs to that later dedicated entitlement/
  redemption persistence design;
  do not assume it works by "clearing" a stored binding. Final operation-ID
  field, retry-token format, JSON payload, and endpoint response schema are
  not defined in this pass.
- Integration contracts (Android wire format, DTOs, game codes) must remain
  versionable/extensible (BR-045) — not defined in this pass.

## Platform Hardening

- Unauthenticated `/wp/v2/users` is disabled network-wide (prevents hall staff
  username enumeration).
